From 62471825bf61b4ee04fcb9582c363e23ec3d4de3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:18:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/40] Recover 64 stub bodies from the reference kernel image

Disassembly-driven reconstruction of the smallest recovered functions:

- 16 immediate-return void bodies and 11 NULL-pointer getters in the
  PPL/exclaves/APT stubs, plus three zero-returning integer helpers.
- Five KERN_NOT_SUPPORTED and two KERN_FAILURE returns (exclaves
  surface root, DRAM ECC, APT external entry points).
- All 19 sptm_gen3dart_* unsupported paths recover the exact panic
  format string, function name, file and line (42-60).
- image4_v2_interface_register: single-assignment interface pointer
  with the reference "already set" panic at line 13.
- hv_trap_vm_{map,unmap,protect}: tail calls into
  hv_space_map_op_nested with selectors 0xc6000015-17.
- hv_trap_vcpu_sysregs_sync: HV_NO_DEVICE when the current thread has
  no hv_thread_target.
- ecc_panic_non_acc and APT no-op/zero-fill helpers.

Remaining explicit stubs: 309 (from 373).

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
---
